  "body": "Synapse Version: 1.83.0\r\nOS: Debian 11 5.10.0-22-amd64\r\n\r\nI just setup the structured log formatting sending logs remotely to Graylog using the \"synapse.logging.TerseJsonFormatter\" following the config provided in https://matrix-org.github.io/synapse/develop/structured_logging.html\r\nUnfortunately, none of the synapse.access.http logs are in JSON format. \r\n\r\nI think it would be extremely useful to have these HTTP logs put in JSON format to make it easier to parse the logs.\r\n\r\nCurrent Log format:\r\n```\r\nMay 17 10:47:28 chat matrix-synapse[147051]: INFO:synapse.access.https.8443:192.168.99.99 - 8443 - {@user:chat.domain.com} Processed request: 0.002sec/0.000sec (0.001sec, 0.000sec) (0.000sec/0.001sec/2) 469B 200 \"GET /_matrix/client/r0/devices HTTP/1.0\" \"Element/1.5.32 (Google Pixel 5; Android 13; TQ2A.230505.002.2023050500; Flavour GooglePlay; MatrixAndroidSdk2 1.5.32)\" [0 dbevts]\r\n```\r\n\r\nExample JSON format:\r\n```\r\n{\"LogLevel\":\"INFO\",\"Log\":\"synapse.access.https.8443\",\"ClientIP\":\"192.168.99.99\",\"Username\":\"@user\",\"UserDomain\":\"chat.domain.com\",\"RequestProcessTime1\":0.002,\"RequestProcessTime2\":0.001,\"RequestProcessTime2\":0.000,\"RequestLength\":469,\"ResponseCode\":200,\"FullRequest\":\"GET /_matrix/client/r0/devices HTTP/1.0\",\"UserAgent\":\"Element/1.5.32 (Google Pixel 5; Android 13; TQ2A.230505.002.2023050500; Flavour GooglePlay; MatrixAndroidSdk2 1.5.32)\"}\r\n```\r\n",
